  "body": "## What to build\n\nExpose the component library, compatibility queries, and assembly commands through MCP in `crates/app/src/mcp/`.\n\n1. Add read and query tools:\n   - `list_tool_components`: lists built-in, user-library, and document components with filters for `kind`, `scope`, and `compatible_with` (for example, listing all holders that accept a given insert).\n   - `get_tool_assembly`: returns a document tool's component stack, ports, Z-rotations, stickout projection, derived cutting parameters, gauge length, and library sync status.\n2. Add document write tools (calling the same undoable commands as the GUI):\n   - `upsert_tool_component`\n   - `delete_tool_component`\n   - `set_tool_assembly`\n   - `sync_tool_component`\n3. Add user-library tools:\n   - `save_library_component`\n   - `delete_library_component`\n4. Update `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` to document the new MCP tools.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Depends on the document commands and persistence sub-issues of #2452.\n- Every tool validates its arguments strictly and refuses unknown keys or incompatible components by name.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests in `crates/app/tests/` cover `list_tool_components` with `compatible_with`, building an assembly with `set_tool_assembly`, editing a shared insert with `upsert_tool_component`, `sync_tool_component`, `undo`/`redo`, and named refusals.\n- `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` lists every new MCP tool.\n\nPart of #2452\n",
